     ccoorreetteemmpp — device driver for Intel Core on-die digital thermal sensor

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ccoorreetteemmpp

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           coretemp_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccoorreetteemmpp driver provides support for the on-die digital thermal sen‐
     sor present in Intel Core and newer CPUs.

     The ccoorreetteemmpp driver reports each core's temperature through a sysctl node
     in the corresponding CPU device's sysctl tree, named
     _d_e_v_._c_p_u_._%_d_._t_e_m_p_e_r_a_t_u_r_e.

